From 815afba3ea32ea75a40ece747d230b4db4584b16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shibco <cade@parare.al>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:58:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] converge on a foreign quantum: predict, adopt, mute

Issue #49 (ableton-linux): a foreign forced quantum (global
clock.force-quantum from pipewire-jack, or another client's
node.force-quantum winning last-change arbitration) leaves the driver
feeding buffer_size frames per quantum-sized cycle: wrong-speed playback
with periodic waveform steps.

Predict: track the settings metadata's global clock.force-quantum;
GetBufferSize and buffer sizing offer it so the host builds matching
buffers from the start. Adopt: the config watcher withdraws our
node.force-quantum after two consecutive mismatched polls and asks the
host to rebuild at the observed quantum (3 adoptions/minute cap).
Mute: while sizes disagree the process path swaps silence both ways, so
the audible fault is silence plus one log line per episode.
PIPEASIO_ALLOW_QUANTUM_MISMATCH=on restores warn-and-play-on.

Port buffers range up to the accepted maximum so a larger foreign
quantum always has a buffer to land in. WoW64 proxy gains the three
calls (PAU_GLOBAL_FORCE_QUANTUM/QUANTUM_MUTED/DROP_FORCE_QUANTUM).
